hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1612","Narrated to us Salm ibn Junādah, narrated to us Wakīʿ, from Jaʿfar ibn Ḥayyān Abū al-Ashhab al-Saʿdī.

And narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Maʿmar al-Qaysī, narrated to us Abū ʿĀmir, who informed us Abū al-Ashhab, who narrated to us Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (RA), who said:
The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) saw some delay in his Companions (RA), so he said:
""Move forward, follow my lead, and let those who come after you follow your lead. The people will continue to fall behind until Allāh causes them to fall behind.""

This is the narration of Wakīʿ.

Ibn Maʿmar said: ""From Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī.""

---
**CHAPTER:**"
